@DMR_HostAddress = http://localhost:5135
@DMR_MasterKey = dmr_7aQW5mKqTibXCerrOu6I5lLoZ8-KJi4LQgvAGZwnrlM

### Every endpoint requires a valid API key (master key or one issued via /Key/Create) in X-Api-Key.

# KeyController — master key only (see services/identity/docs). Action-routed: /Key/<Action>[/{id}].

### Create a new API key. The raw key is only ever shown in this response.
POST {{DMR_HostAddress}}/Key/Create
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{DMR_MasterKey}}

{
  "name": "example client",
  "contactInfo": "someone@example.com",
  "expiresAtUtc": null
}

###

### List active keys (add ?includeRevoked=true to also see revoked ones).
GET {{DMR_HostAddress}}/Key/List
X-Api-Key: {{DMR_MasterKey}}

###

### Roll a key over: issues fresh secret material for it (old raw key stops working immediately) while
### keeping its id, name, contact info, expiry and usage history. Replace {id} with a real key id.
POST {{DMR_HostAddress}}/Key/Rollover/{id}
X-Api-Key: {{DMR_MasterKey}}

###

### Revoke a key by id (replace {id} with a real key id from a create/list response).
DELETE {{DMR_HostAddress}}/Key/Revoke/{id}
X-Api-Key: {{DMR_MasterKey}}

###
